<Base title="About This Site | Passport Office Finder" desc="What Passport Office Finder is, where the data comes from, and why we are not the U.S. Department of State.">
<main class="wrap">
  <h1 style="font-size:1.7rem">About this site</h1>
  <p class="lead">Passport Office Finder is a <strong>private, independent</strong> reference site about applying for U.S. passports. We are not affiliated with the U.S. Department of State, USPS, or any government agency.</p>
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>We organize public data: the State Department's official database of passport acceptance facilities (all of them, with phones, hours and services), the addresses of the 27 regional agencies from their official pages, and the current fee schedule — into pages that answer real questions directly. Everything is free.</p>
  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Book appointments, accept applications, or handle documents — facilities and travel.state.gov do that.</li>
    <li>Sell expediting services or charge for anything.</li>
    <li>Collect your personal or passport information.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Sources and methodology</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Facility directory:</strong> the State Department's public facility locator database, refreshed periodically. Service badges (accessibility, on-site photos) come from the same official data.</li>
    <li><strong>Agencies:</strong> each agency's official travel.state.gov page.</li>
    <li><strong>Fees and timelines:</strong> the official fee schedule; verified at publication and marked with update dates. When processing times fluctuate, we say so and point to the live official estimate.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Funding</h2>
  <p>The site is supported by advertising (Google AdSense), clearly distinguishable from content and with no influence on it.</p>
</main>
</Base>
